    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Spanish long‑form possessive adjectives agree with the noun they modify in gender and number. Forms include *mío/mía/míos/mías* ('mine'), *tuyo/tuya/…* ('yours'), *suyo/suya/…* ('yours/his/her/theirs') and *nuestro/nuestra/nuestros/nuestras* ('ours'). \nThese adjectives typically follow the noun or appear after the verb *ser*, as in *Estos libros son nuestros*. When the context does not make the reference clear, alternative constructions using *de* (e.g., *el libro de Juan*) are preferred to avoid ambiguity."
    }
